### R1. Corrections to the inventory

- **Accepted corrections to C.** I omitted a consequence of ordinary RH: genus‑2 factoring discharges SNFS cofactor recognition (O2). Pointwise smooth supply (O1) and the certification bookkeeping remain. G also correctly adds the \(L[2/5]\) extension of ZA, the implication from IW circuit hardness once Dirichlet GRH is granted, and the randomized one-call successor reduction. [SNFS:601](/Volumes/git/factoring-connection/notes/snfsrig_results.md:601) · [ZA:295](/Volumes/git/factoring-connection/notes/zroute_results.md:295) · [IWD:189](/Volumes/git/factoring-connection/notes/dsr_results.md:189) · [Successor:128](/Volumes/git/factoring-connection/notes/factorbits_results.md:128)
- **Accepted with scope.** G’s additional odd-index, S-unit determinant, collision-count, navigation and residue-barrier entries belong in the inventory. NAV’s square/unit conversion retains \(2^{\omega(N)}\le y^{1/2-\varepsilon}\), and its discrete-log reduction concerns a sufficiently fast uniform navigator. GEN decides **principal-genus membership**. Finding an ambiguous form is a different task. [Odd index:81](/Volumes/git/factoring-connection/notes/schnorrcvp_results.md:81) · [S-units:82](/Volumes/git/factoring-connection/notes/abcsunit_results.md:82) · [NAV:124](/Volumes/git/factoring-connection/notes/navigate_results.md:124) · [DL reduction:52](/Volumes/git/factoring-connection/notes/navigate_results.md:52) · [Residues:380](/Volumes/git/factoring-connection/notes/selfred_results.md:380) · [GEN:159](/Volumes/git/factoring-connection/notes/genusleak_results.md:159)
- **Hypothesis corrections.** The remark leaves its GRH family unspecified. Bruin explicitly assumes RH for number-field zeta functions. Lemma \(X_{\rm ERH}\) invokes both \(\zeta_K\) and the extension zetas. Younis’s unrefereed status is a verification issue, not an additional conjecture: both genus‑2 constants lose their sole zero hypothesis under RH, and both retain internal accounting. Theorem R returns a **proper divisor**. The \(L[1/2]\) limitation inferred from Arakelov sampling is expressly heuristic. [Remark p. 1](https://alpo.ge/remark.pdf) · [Bruin](https://www.numdam.org/item/10.5802/pmb.a-133.pdf) · [Factored input:569](/Volumes/git/factoring-connection/notes/nativemod_results.md:569) · [\(X_{\rm ERH}\):426](/Volumes/git/factoring-connection/notes/nested_results.md:426) · [Theorem R:9](/Volumes/git/factoring-connection/notes/genus2rh_results.md:9) · [Arakelov comparison:62](/Volumes/git/factoring-connection/notes/nested_results.md:62)
- **Other overstatements.** GRH removes the exceptional character in Hyp SC; a smooth-character estimate still does work. NR drops FM and LD*. Published external inputs leave the \(U'\)-under-DW proof outstanding. Batch Conjecture F differs from LV 7.1. GRH’s small-witness bounds do not give Burgess improvements for arbitrary shifted, smooth-weighted intervals. G’s diagonal-noise explanation for Prop SI is conjectural. The \(a_f(N)\) bound sharpens a **model** parameter, and \(N^{1/2+o(1)}\) prices surveyed native methods. Neither that survey nor the phase-discarding barriers establish general impossibility. [SC:333](/Volumes/git/factoring-connection/notes/mf2L_results.md:333) · [NR:113](/Volumes/git/factoring-connection/notes/nested_results.md:113) · [Audit:76](/Volumes/git/factoring-connection/notes/audit2L_audit.md:76) · [F versus 7.1:426](/Volumes/git/factoring-connection/notes/nfsfruit_results.md:426) · [Shifted sums:313](/Volumes/git/factoring-connection/notes/nfsfruit_results.md:313) · [Analytic survey:23](/Volumes/git/factoring-connection/notes/conn_ana.md:23) · [Trace model:196](/Volumes/git/factoring-connection/notes/cuspcoef_results.md:196) · [Phase restriction:305](/Volumes/git/factoring-connection/notes/cov38b_results.md:305)

### R2. The three proposals

**(a) Pooled LV relations — valid conditional reduction, speculative 1% for the missing theorem in 4–8 weeks.** The orchestrator is right about Miller. Given a genuine \(\lambda(N)\)-multiple, random bases split unconditionally. GRH matters one step earlier: pinning the small primes proves their orders divide the computed minor, and Bach makes those primes generate the whole unit group. The missing lemma is that for **every preprocessed \(N\)**, an \(L[1/3,O(1)]\)-cost batch of LV fields has, with sufficient probability for that expected budget, \(e_q\in\sum_j W_j\) for **every** required small prime. Each \(W_j\) must come from exact ideal and unit cancellation **within field \(j\)**. One row per field can cover every target while every \(W_j=0\). This serves the same algorithmic purpose as fruitfulness, but parity rank and exact rational rank are incomparable. The remark contributes no rank estimate. [Random split:202](/Volumes/git/factoring-connection/notes/systeq_results.md:202) · [PIN:211](/Volumes/git/factoring-connection/notes/zroute_results.md:211) · [Pooling counterexample:312](/Volumes/git/factoring-connection/notes/zroute_results.md:312) · [Rank comparison:367](/Volumes/git/factoring-connection/notes/zroute_results.md:367)

**(b) Bost slopes — plausible barrier research, speculative 3% for closure in 1–3 months.** RR charges \(e\log N/d\). G needs a charge growing with \(r=me\), uniform in \(m\), for non-power generators. There is a further quantitative flaw: at the proposed \(L[1/4]\) balance, writing \(x=\log N\), G’s main term \(rx/D\) has order \(x^{3/4}\), while its allowed \(O(dn)\) error has order \(x\) for fixed \(e\). The bound can be vacuous. The missing lemma is a relative R1 estimate with smaller error **and** control of how many independent low-norm box points survive unit action and archimedean cancellation. The suggested Gaussian example uses \(1,s,s^2\), a power basis. It checks RR but misses the non-power case. [Scaling and box counts:35](/Volumes/git/factoring-connection/notes/grdeg_results.md:35) · [RR:143](/Volumes/git/factoring-connection/notes/grdeg_results.md:143) · [Witness:264](/Volumes/git/factoring-connection/notes/grdeg_results.md:264)

**(c) \(4/11\) variance — borderline in the model, speculative 3% for the endpoint estimate in 4–8 weeks.** G identifies the right source of drift but reverses the inequality. LF‑A and OPV‑A prove **upper** bounds in the two-level design. Neither proves an \(\Omega(D^{-2\alpha})\) floor at depth three. The missing lemma controls the incidence-weighted, conditioned principal terms and character errors together so that \(\phi_2\le\eta_2\) and \(\sigma_2^2\phi_2\lesssim\eta_2^2\), with \(\eta_2\asymp D^{-2\alpha}\) and constants sufficient for decoupling. My earlier ranking gave spectral positivity too much weight. The explicit formula supplies no centering identity for the archimedean density or gcd factor. [LF‑A:379](/Volumes/git/factoring-connection/notes/thmAB_results.md:379) · [OPV‑A:400](/Volumes/git/factoring-connection/notes/thmAB_results.md:400) · [Depth model:348](/Volumes/git/factoring-connection/notes/pc3_results.md:348)

### R3. Verdict and priorities

No verified construction beats \(L[1/3]\). Relative-rank‑\(\ge3\) type‑D families remain a concrete opening, with \(L[1/4]\) conditional even as a model prediction. The remark supplies no construction there. [Frontier:66](/Volumes/git/factoring-connection/notes/grdeg_results.md:66)

1. **Finish the \(3/8\) proof**, including \(U'\) under DW and the parent-filter repair. **60%, 2–4 researcher-weeks.** [Audit:76](/Volumes/git/factoring-connection/notes/audit2L_audit.md:76)
2. **Resolve the \(4/11\) endpoint variance estimate** in R2(c). **3%, 4–8 weeks.**
3. **Test type‑D in both directions** with growing rank and non-power generators. **3% for barrier closure, under 1% for a useful construction, 1–3 months.**